```c
/**
 * Construct the path to the block file holding a given position.
 *
 * @param name on input, the root of the tree (the exportname); on
 * output, the full path of the block file
 * @param lenmax size of the name buffer
 * @param size total size of the export
 * @param pos position within the export
 * @param ppos out: offset of pos within the block file
 */
void construct_path(char *name, int lenmax, off_t size, off_t pos, off_t *ppos) {
	off_t nr = pos / TREEPAGESIZE;
	off_t cnt = (size + TREEPAGESIZE - 1) / TREEPAGESIZE;
	off_t div = 1;
	int len;
	char *c = name + strlen(name);

	assert(pos >= 0);
	assert(pos < size);

	*ppos = pos % TREEPAGESIZE;

	/* compute the depth of the tree we need: the number of
	 * directory levels required to store cnt block files with at
	 * most TREEDIRSIZE entries per directory */
	while (cnt > TREEDIRSIZE) {
		cnt = (cnt + TREEDIRSIZE - 1) / TREEDIRSIZE;
		div *= TREEDIRSIZE;
	}

	/* nr = dir_1 * div + ... ; write out the directory components
	 * from most significant to least significant */
	while (div > 1) {
		div /= TREEDIRSIZE;
		len = snprintf(c, lenmax - (c - name), "/%04X", (unsigned int)((nr / div) % TREEDIRSIZE));
		...
	}
	snprintf(c, ..., "/%04X", (unsigned int)(nr % TREEDIRSIZE));
}
```

Wait, I need to be careful with the computation of depth and div. Let me define it like this:
- depth = the number of directory levels (directories only). depth=0 → all block files are directly under root.
- Total capacity at depth d: TREEDIRSIZE^(d+1) blocks.
- Loop: `while (cnt > TREEDIRSIZE) { cnt = ceil(cnt / TREEDIRSIZE); div *= TREEDIRSIZE; }` — each iteration adds one level. div ends up = TREEDIRSIZE^depth.

Example: cnt=1024 → no iterations, depth=0, div=1. Path: only leaf file "/%04X" (nr%1024). Good.
cnt=1025 → 1 iteration: cnt=2, div=1024. nr is in range [0,1025). div=1024: top-level directory index = (nr/1024)%1024 = 0 or 1. Then the leaf = nr%1024. Good.
cnt=1048577 (=1024²+1) → iteration 1: cnt=1025, div=1024; iteration 2: cnt=2, div=1024². Components: (nr/div)%1024, then div/=1024 → (nr/1024)%1024, leaf nr%1024. Good.

Loop to write components:
```c
while (div > 0) {
    len = snprintf(c, rem, "/%04X", (unsigned)((nr / div) % TREEDIRSIZE));
    c += len; 
    div /= TREEDIRSIZE;
}
```
When div starts at TREEDIRSIZE^depth: when div=1024^depth → digit d_depth ... down to div=1 → digit d_0 (leaf). So a single loop handles both the directories and the leaf! When div=1: (nr/1)%1024 = d_0, then div=0 → stop.

So:
```c
while (div > 0) {
	int w = snprintf(c, lenmax - (c - name), "/%04X", (unsigned int)((nr / div) % TREEDIRSIZE));
	if (w < 0 || w >= lenmax - (c - name)) {
		DEBUG("construct_path: buffer too small\n");
		exit? abort? 
	}
	c += w;
	div /= TREEDIRSIZE;
}
```

